id: pm-rl-8nev
title: Stabilize Compose cancellation barrier diagnostics under shared host load
description: "The existing cancellation-plus-cleanup-failure drill missed its partial-artifact barrier during concurrent package validation, then reported the wall watchdog refusal. Preserve current bounds while making trainer startup, timeout attribution and cleanup deterministic under shared host load. This predates the LM integration; its full release gate will independently verify the unchanged case."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#107"
created_at: "2026-10-15T22:23:36.056Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T16:38:52.255Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce the startup/barrier timing condition with real containers, retain cleanup evidence and distinguish startup delay from a trainer cancellation failure without weakening resource or coverage limits."
parent: pm-rl-mjo5
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T23:18:24.790Z",codex-agent,"The failed full Bun attempt reported Container did not publish its partial artifact in the existing orphan-recovery drill. It began the 15-second partial-artifact polling interval after first seeing a planned reservation, while the controller still committed its running transition. The revised drill waits on the existing real running-write IPC barrier, reads the job once, then starts the unchanged trainer startup barrier. Tighten fixture matching to a full process job ID so the loop collection step cannot satisfy the running barrier. Keep the 15-second barrier, 30-second trainer allowance and every orphan/recovery/accounting assertion; always kill the owned controller and clean its job container on assertion failure."
  "2026-10-15T23:26:52.822Z",codex-agent,"The lifecycle-barrier drill passed under coverage directly (1/1) and through pm test pm-rl-8nev --run --progress (1/1, case 46658.868 ms, zero skips). An isolated check restoring the old broad fixture-ID predicate also passed (1/1, 51304.099 ms), so the extra predicate change was dropped; it is not claimed as a behavioural revert proof. The final test waits on the existing running-job barrier before the unchanged 15-second trainer-startup interval, reads the reservation once, and always cleans its owned controller/container. The observed failure was the startup-artifact assertion; no production recovery defect was demonstrated. Test image builds now use unique worker names/labels so cleanup cannot remove a peer validation image."
  "2026-10-16T03:47:17.620Z",codex-agent,"Final verification: both complete npm and Bun release gates pass 590/590, zero skips, 100% across all four coverage dimensions. The real orphan drill passes in both. The fixture observes the persisted running state before the unchanged partial-artifact interval and preserves all SIGKILL, no-relaunch, retained-evidence and settlement assertions. Owned cleanup is verified; leave open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-24T21:47:39.081Z",codex-agent,"Returned to open in the 2026-10-24 sweep: Recorded receipts show an improved running-state barrier, but no merged PR claim or item-comment delivery link establishes attribution for this record. Retain the real-container acceptance for review; no active work."
  "2026-10-30T14:56:12.002Z",codex-agent,"Review-round gate reproduced controller-readiness failures on both the current patch and untouched cd91de9. The fixture observes client.update, while transitionProcessJob now commits through SDK mutateItem, so running/materialized barriers are not observed. Migrate only fixture synchronization to the existing ProcessCoordinates.onTransition observer: prepared before materialization and step_applied after forward state writes. Keep the planned-create barrier, native records, crash assertions, limits and timeouts. This is gate-fixture work required by pm-rl-sequential, not a change to process mutation or recovery behavior."
  "2026-10-30T15:00:40.516Z",codex-agent,"Original fixture controls fail 0/3 on cd91de9 and 0/3 on the review patch: concurrency, SIGKILL before materialization commit and orphan-trainer recovery all exit before the missing IPC barrier. The fixture-only observer migration restores 3/3, zero skips: concurrency retains one launch/reservation, staged completion survives SIGKILL without relaunch, and orphan recovery stops the trainer while retaining artifacts. Public ProcessCoordinates.onTransition is the existing SDK-backed capability; no SDK mocks, new production hooks, allowance changes or timeout changes. Production code remains unchanged by this gate repair. Starting a fresh complete gate with the corrected fixture; the superseded partial full run is not acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-30T15:15:39.269Z",codex-agent,"Remaining production follow-up outside the seven requested findings: all four existing Compose cleanup-diagnostic cases refuse process_job_drift. executeReservedProcessJob adds the desired cleanup diagnostic to its job argument before transitionProcessJob compares that argument with the current native record; the saved-base and desired-state documents are therefore conflated. A correction must keep the real saved base and monotonic revision separate from the desired diagnostic, without weakening peer-conflict checks or rolling back state. The fixture-only barrier repair is verified 3/3 directly and through pm test (snapshot/PM context none). Keep this production blocker visible; full release attempts are not reported as passing."
  "2026-10-30T15:26:17.867Z",codex-agent,"Original-head control confirms all four cleanup-diagnostic tests also fail on untouched cd91de9 (0/4, zero skips), with process_job_drift before settlement. Current review code reproduces the same 0/4. This confirms a pre-existing production blocker, distinct from the repaired fixture barriers. A follow-up must separate actual saved state from desired cleanup annotations rather than relaxing revision or whole-document checks."
  "2026-10-30T16:38:52.254Z",codex-agent,"The native cleanup controls also reproduce on untouched cd91de9: test/controller-boundaries.test.ts selection executes 12 tests, 2 pass and 10 fail, zero skips. Current code reports the same process_job_drift before settlement in the owned-stop and cleanup-exhaustion cases. These share the saved-base/desired-cleanup conflation with the four Compose failures; the seven-thread review does not change process.ts or relax that guard."
